 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Polarity and direction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A-suffix parts are unidirectional, with the band marking the cathode. CA-suffix parts are bidirectional, carry no band, and hold the same electrical figures for either polarity. Forward surge figures (IFSM, fig. 6) and the forward voltage of 3.5 V at 100 A apply to unidirectional parts only."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Pulse rating",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "The 1500 W rating is for a 10/1000 µs pulse: 10 µs rise to the peak, decaying to half the peak at 1000 µs (fig. 3), repeated at a duty cycle of no more than 0.01 %. Shorter pulses allow more peak power and longer ones less (fig. 1): about 100 kW at 0.1 µs, falling to about 0.55 kW near 10 ms, with each terminal on an 8.0 x 8.0 mm copper pad. The electrical table gives each part's maximum clamping voltage VC at its IPPM, a 10/1000 µs pulse."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Derating with temperature",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Peak pulse power and current hold their full value up to an initial junction temperature of 25 °C, then the safe operating limit falls linearly to zero at 150 °C (fig. 2). The typical curve falls less steeply, to about 65 % at 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Steady dissipation is 6.5 W on an infinite heatsink at TA = 50 °C. Junction to leads is 15 °C/W and junction to ambient 75 °C/W on the minimum recommended pads; the transient thermal impedance rises from about 0.2 °C/W at 1 ms to settle near 75 °C/W beyond a few hundred seconds (fig. 5)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Capacitance",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Junction capacitance falls with rated voltage and with applied bias (fig. 4). At zero bias a unidirectional part is roughly 10 nF near 6 V stand-off and about 600 pF at 200 V; biased at its stand-off voltage it is about 2.2 nF at 10 V and about 130 pF at 200 V. Bidirectional parts at zero bias run from about 8.5 nF at 5 V to about 140 pF at 220 V, and at stand-off bias from about 5.9 nF at 4 V to about 94 pF at 250 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Mechanical and qualification",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Glass-passivated chip in a low-profile SMC (DO-214AB) moulded case meeting UL 94 V-0. Terminals are matte tin, solderable to J-STD-002 and JESD 22-B102; E3, M3, HE3 and HM3 finishes pass the JESD 201 class 2 whisker test. Moisture sensitivity level 1 to J-STD-020, with a lead-free peak of 260 °C. HE3 and HM3 codes are AEC-Q101 qualified; E3 and M3 are commercial grade, M3 and HM3 halogen-free. Unit weight 0.211 g."
  }
 ],
